' ======================
' ENTITY RELATIONSHIPS
' ======================
User "1" -- "0..1" Company : recruiter
note on link
  cascade delete
  unique: recruiter_user_id
end note

' User -> CandidateProfile (1 to 0..1)
User "1" -- "0..1" CandidateProfile : owns
note on link
  cascade delete
  unique: user_id
end note

' User -> Resume (1 to *)
User "1" -- "*" Resume : creates
note on link
  cascade delete
  user_id: FK
end note

' User -> JobPosting (1 to *)
User "1" -- "*" JobPosting : posts
note on link
  cascade delete
  recruiter_user_id: FK
end note

' User -> Application (1 to *)
User "1" -- "*" Application : applies
note on link
  cascade delete
  candidate_user_id: FK
end note

' User -> OtpCode (1 to *)
User "1" -- "*" OtpCode : requests
note on link
  cascade set null
  user_id: FK nullable
end note

' User -> AuditLog (1 to *)
User "1" -- "*" AuditLog : acts
note on link
  cascade delete
  actor_user_id: FK
end note

' Company -> JobPosting (1 to *)
Company "1" -- "*" JobPosting : posts jobs
note on link
  cascade delete
  company_id: FK
end note

' Category -> Tag (1 to *)
Category "1" -- "*" Tag : categorizes
note on link
  cascade delete
  category_id: FK
end note

' Tag <-> JobPosting (many to many)
Tag "*" -- "*" JobPosting : tags
(Tag,JobPosting) .. JobTag_Junction : uses

' Tag <-> Resume (many to many)
Tag "*" -- "*" Resume : skills
(Tag,Resume) .. ResumeTag_Junction : uses

' JobPosting -> Application (1 to *)
JobPosting "1" -- "*" Application : has applications
note on link
  cascade delete
  job_id: FK
end note

' JobPosting -> MatchScore (1 to *)
JobPosting "1" -- "*" MatchScore : scored against
note on link
  cascade delete
  job_id: FK
end note

' Resume -> Application (1 to *)
Resume "1" -- "*" Application : submitted in
note on link
  cascade delete
  resume_id: FK
end note

' Resume -> MatchScore (1 to *)
Resume "1" -- "*" MatchScore : matched with
note on link
  cascade delete
  resume_id: FK
end note

' Application -> CandidateProfile (via User)
Application -- CandidateProfile : candidate

' MatchScore -> CandidateProfile (via User)
MatchScore -- CandidateProfile : candidate profile

' OtpCode - CvTemplate (no direct relation, but both used in authentication/CV creation flow)

' ======================
' NOTES
' ======================

note bottom of User
  **Roles & Responsibilities:**
  - admin: quản lý hệ thống
  - recruiter: đăng tin tuyển dụng
  - candidate: ứng tuyển
  
  **Methods:**
  - is_recruiter(), is_candidate(), is_admin()
  - verify_password(), set_password()
  - check_is_authenticated()
end note

note bottom of Resume
  **Source Types:**
  - manual: tạo từ template
  - upload: upload file CV
  
  **Formats:**
  - PDF, DOCX, hoặc cả hai
  - Lưu raw text, JSON, PDF, DOCX
  
  **Operations:**
  - add_tag(), remove_tag()
  - generate_pdf(), generate_docx()
  - set_as_primary()
end note

note bottom of Application
  **Workflow:**
  1. Candidate chọn Resume
  2. Submit hồ sơ cho JobPosting
  3. Recruiter review & update status
  4. Candidate withdraw hoặc accepted/rejected
  
  **Business Logic:**
  - Can only apply once per job
  - Status transitions must be valid
  - Notifications sent on status change
end note

note bottom of MatchScore
  **Scoring Logic:**
  - So sánh Tags của Job vs Resume
  - Breakdown JSON: chi tiết scoring
  - Score: 0-100 hoặc 0-1
end note

note right of OtpCode
  **Purpose:**
  - register: đăng ký tài khoản
  - login: xác thực đăng nhập
  - reset: reset password
  
  **Security:**
  - Lưu code_hash (không plain text)
  - Max attempts: 5
  - Expiration: 5 phút
  - Resend delay: 60 phút
end note

note bottom of AuditLog
  **Audit Trail:**
  - Log tất cả thay đổi dữ liệu
  - Lưu before/after JSON
  - IP tracking
  - Dùng cho compliance
end note

note bottom of BaseModel
  **Base Model Pattern:**
  - All entities inherit from BaseModel
  - Common attributes: id, created_at, updated_at
  - Common methods: save(), delete(), to_dict()
  - Provides ORM layer abstraction
end note

note bottom of BaseService
  **Service Layer Pattern:**
  - Encapsulates business logic
  - Coordinates multiple repositories
  - Handles validation and error handling
  - Provides transaction management
  
  **Separation of Concerns:**
  - Services: Business logic
  - Repositories: Data access
  - Models: Data structure
end note

note bottom of BaseRepository
  **Repository Pattern:**
  - Abstraction over data access
  - Standard CRUD operations
  - Query methods for domain operations
  - Decouples from database implementation
  
  **Benefits:**
  - Easy to test with mock repositories
  - Database agnostic
  - Centralized query logic
end note

note left of AuthenticationService
  **OOP Design Patterns Used:**
  
  1. **Inheritance:**
     - All Services extend BaseService
     - All Repositories extend BaseRepository
     - All Models extend BaseModel
  
  2. **Composition:**
     - Services depend on Repositories
     - Services may depend on other Services
     - Promotes loose coupling
  
  3. **Dependency Injection:**
     - Repositories injected into Services
     - Services injected into Controllers
  
  4. **Abstraction:**
     - BaseService/BaseRepository
     - Interface-like behavior
  
  5. **Encapsulation:**
     - Private methods (#)
     - Protected repositories
     - Public API methods (+)
end note

@enduml
